WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.767
You're here. You made it.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.167
Well, you guys, I want to wish everyone here

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.167
a very happy St. Patrick's Day.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:14.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:16.801
Yeah, it's a great day to be Irish

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:19.767
and a bad day to be an Uber driver.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.434
That's right. It's St. Patrick's Day.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:24.033
That's why our guest tonight is renowned Irish Catholic

00:00:24.033 --> 00:00:25.767
Billy Crystal, is here tonight.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.767
[ Cheers and applause ] That's right.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:31.234
[ Chuckles ] But this is exciting.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:33.801
After a two-year hiatus, the St. Patrick's Day Parade

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.167
finally returned to New York City.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:40.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.334
You can tell people were ready to let loose.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.067
On my way in, I heard a guy on the street

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.934
ask where the bathrooms are, and another guy said,

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.400
"It's wherever you want it to be."

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.334
And I said, "Wow. We're back."

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.100
Yep, the parade here is the only event

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.467
where Times Square Elmo feels like the chaperone.

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.167
It was fun seeing everyone decked out

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.734
in their St. Patty's Day clothes.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:03.400
Some people wore shirts that said, "Kiss me. I'm Irish."

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.000
While the rest opted for the newer,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.801
"Kiss me. Rapid's negative."

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.634
And you know what I saw online today?

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.400
Did you guys hear about this? There's a company in Boston

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.834
that rents out an inflatable Irish pub

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.834
that can hold up to 80 people.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.868
I got to get this thing. Look at this thing.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:24.000
[ Laughter ] -Oh!

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.901
-How rad is that?

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:29.200
It's the only pub where the bouncer is actually bouncing.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.934
[ Laughter ] And also, no darts.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:34.200
-[ Pop, air hisses ] -Ooh, okay.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.133
Not only -- Mot only is it St. Patrick's Day,

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.434
it's also March Madness,

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.334
and I saw that for the tournament,

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.901
Pizza Hut is bringing back its Big Dinner Box.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.467
Look at this thing. Yeah. Wow.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:48.100
It's perfect for the tournament because if you eat that alone,

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.067
your life expectancy goes from 64 to 32

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:54.734
to 16 to 8 to...

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.801
Meanwhile, Coors Light is selling a six-pack

00:01:56.801 --> 00:02:00.834
of beer-flavored lollipops to fans during March Madness.

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.667
Look at this thing. Yeah. Oh, I love it.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:06.100
I love it. It's never too early to introduce your kids

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.100
to the cold, refreshing taste of Coors Light.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.200
The lollipops don't actually have any alcohol in them,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.801
and people were like, "Yeah, we figured that

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.667
when you said Coors Light."

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:18.634
-Oy! -Switching gears...

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:22.267
I read that Netflix is trying to crack down on password sharing

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:26.434
by charging an extra fee to users who share their account.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:28.834
In other words, everyone under 30

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:31.033
is about to find out that Netflix isn't free.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.434
Yeah. "What?"

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.367
And if you don't pay the extra fee,

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.400
they're threatening to make this 14 times louder.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.634
[ Netflix start-up tones play ]

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:39.834
"Okay! All right! I'll pay it! I'll pay it!"

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.567
It's frightening enough.

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.167
Well, listen to this.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:46.467
A man visiting Florida accidentally spent the night

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:49.767
in a stranger's home because he thought it was his Airbnb.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:54.667
The guy apologized then drove away in the stranger's car.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:57.367
He's like, "All right. See you guys later."

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.868
And finally, as I mentioned, today is St. Patrick's Day,

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.367
and everywhere you look there's Irish music and food.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:05.667
But Irish culture isn't just about one day of the year,

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.667
so I thought I'd sing a tiny song about it.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:08.834
I hope you enjoy it.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:21.400
♪ They say that everybody's Irish one day of the year ♪

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.434
♪ But I see Irish everywhere ♪

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:27.133
♪ So put down that green beer ♪

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:28.934
♪♪

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:33.367
♪ Minnesota's where they make your Lucky Charms for you ♪

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:35.400
♪ Bennigan's is from Atlanta ♪

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.267
♪ Germans make O'Doul's ♪

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:40.968
♪ Tom Carvel made Cookie O'Puss here in NYC ♪

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:43.200
♪ And Shamrock Shakes are from Chicago ♪

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.834
♪ Home of Mickey D's ♪

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:48.701
♪ So while you swing shillelaghs singing hi-dee-ti-dee-ti ♪

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:52.634
♪ Remember "Danny Boy" was written by an English guy ♪

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:54.434
♪ The Riddler's green, but that don't mean ♪

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.367
♪ He comes from the Isle ♪

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:58.200
♪ 'Cause fiddling's more the Penguin's thing ♪

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.200
♪ When Colin Farrell smiles ♪

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.367
♪ And if you're asked if someone's Irish ♪

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.167
♪ Or what their deal is ♪

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.133
♪ Tell them Julianne Moore isn't ♪

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:07.767
♪ But Shaquille O'Neal is ♪

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:11.534
♪ 'Cause Irish isn't wearing green or having orange hair ♪

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:15.300
♪ St. Patrick's Day and every day, it's Irish everywhere ♪

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.801
We have a great show!

